integrated_rules:
If (A) socialist-leaning policy tools have already proven workable and publicly accepted within the US system AND (B) adopting additional socialist reforms is feasible within the US without requiring that capitalism be eliminated AND (C) increasing socialist redistribution directly remedies severe wealth inequality and its harms AND (D) there is broad popular support for multiple concrete socialist policies, then the policy is supported toward “Yes—become more socialist,” provided that (E) the proposal is not supported by evidence to conflict with promoting equal opportunity; 

If (E) the proposal is supported by evidence to conflict with promoting equal opportunity, then the policy is supported toward “No—do not become more socialist,” even if (A)–(D) hold; 

If the evidence yields both (A)–(D) support and (E) conflict (or neither is clearly established), then the conclusion is unresolved.
